{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nA non-blocking PASS under either engine earns the same certification: a signed plan-review attestation that the claim gate, close gate, `review-plan --status` and `sign-review` accept (ADR 0049). Since [rebar:confident-snooty-stinkpot], an agentic PASS is signed through the same `_finalize_signature` → `attest.sign_plan_review` path, and every agentic verdict carries `coverage.engine = \"agentic\"`; pipeline verdicts carry no `engine` key. The signed manifest does not record which engine produced it, so the two engines cannot be audited side by side once sidecars are pruned (`sidecar.prune`, 50 per ticket).\n\n## Approach\n\n**Signed field.** `manifest.build_manifest` (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/manifest.py:478`) appends `engine: agentic` when the verdict's `coverage.engine` is `\"agentic\"`, the only non-pipeline engine `plan_review.PLAN_REVIEW_ENGINES` defines; any other value writes nothing. A pipeline manifest is byte-identical to today's, so no existing or future pipeline attestation changes. The line is inside the signed bytes (the signature binds `(ticket_id, manifest)`), so editing it breaks verification. Manifest readers already ignore unknown lines (`manifest.py:14`), so claim, close, `--status` and `sign-review` accept the new line unchanged. New reader `manifest_engine(manifest) -> str` returns the line's value when it is a known engine, else `\"pipeline\"`, so every attestation signed before this change reads as pipeline. ADR 0123 §5's `engine` field is thus always readable while pipeline manifests stay byte-identical. No migration. Agentic attestations signed between [rebar:confident-snooty-stinkpot] and this change also read as pipeline. None exist in the shared store: the agentic engine has run only in tests, and the production MCP workspace predates it. `sign-review` restores the line from the sidecar for any that do.\n\n**Carried through every re-sign.**\n- `sign-review` (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/resign.py`) rebuilds the verdict from the stored sidecar, including its `coverage` (`resign.py:337`), and calls `build_manifest`. The agentic sidecar's `coverage.engine` therefore reaches the re-signed manifest with no resign change. A test pins it.\n- `attest.refresh_attestation` (drift refresh) rebuilds the verdict from the prior manifest's fields. It gains `fields[\"coverage\"][\"engine\"] = manifest_engine(prior_manifest)`. A refresh re-binds the PRIOR verdict to current hashes after a cheap probe and never re-reviews, so the engine that produced that verdict is still the right provenance. `manifest_engine` lives in `manifest.py` (709 lines) and, per that module's rule, is re-exported from `attest` (import block and `__all__`). `attest.py` (786 lines) grows by about 3 lines.\n\n**Surfaced.** `attest_gate.plan_review_status` (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest_gate.py:202`) adds `engine`: the signed attestation's `manifest_engine`, or `None` when no readable certified attestation exists, beside `currency_basis`. This one function backs the CLI `review-plan --status` JSON and the MCP `plan_review_status` tool. `src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_status.schema.json` gains the optional `engine` property (`\"pipeline\"`, `\"agentic\"` or null). It stays out of `required`, so older readers are unaffected. `docs/plan-review-gate.md` documents the field.\n\n## Scope\n\n- src/rebar/llm/plan_review/manifest.py (`engine:` line, `manifest_engine`)\n- src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest.py (refresh carries engine)\n- src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest_gate.py (status field)\n- src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_status.schema.json\n- docs/plan-review-gate.md\n- tests/unit/test_plan_review_attest_engine.py (new)\n- tests/unit/test_plan_review_discovery.py (`test_review_plan_status_stays_narrow` key set gains `engine`)\n- tests/unit/test_output_schemas.py (the pinned narrow `PLAN_REVIEW_STATUS` property set gains `engine`, the deliberate reviewable growth that pin asks for)\n\n## Testing\n\nAll tests run offline with a counting FakeRunner and real signing in a temp repo.\n\n- Happy path: an agentic PASS signs a manifest containing `engine: agentic`. `plan_review_status` reports `certified` with `engine == \"agentic\"`, `claim` succeeds, and `_commands.gates.close_plan_review_gate_check` accepts the attestation.\n- Unknown value: a verdict with `coverage.engine == \"other\"` writes no line, and a manifest line `engine: other` reads as `\"pipeline\"`.\n- Re-sign: after the reviewed code drifts, `sign-review` re-certifies the agentic attestation, and the new manifest still carries `engine: agentic`. `refresh_attestation` on an agentic prior manifest also keeps it.\n- Back-compat: a pipeline PASS manifest has no `engine:` line, is byte-identical to the manifest built without the change, and reads as `\"pipeline\"`. `plan_review_status` reports `engine == \"pipeline\"`.\n- Tamper: rewriting `engine: agentic` to `engine: pipeline` in a signed record fails `signing.verify_signature`.\n- Refusal: an agentic BLOCK and an agentic INDETERMINATE write no attestation, and `engine` is `None` on status.\n- `plan_review_status` output validates against `plan_review_status.schema.json` both with `engine` set and with it null.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Agentic PASS attestations record `engine: agentic` inside the signed manifest. Claim, close, `review-plan --status`, `sign-review` and drift refresh accept and preserve it, pinned by `tests/unit/test_plan_review_attest_engine.py`.\n- [ ] Pipeline manifests are byte-identical, and pre-existing attestations without the line read as `\"pipeline\"`, pinned by the back-compat test.\n- [ ] Tampering with the field fails signature verification, pinned by the tamper test.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1794464229956321001,"uuid":"07cd192a-0283-4e5c-b89f-d54d4aa2bc65"}